    "body": "_Requested by **Sia** · follow-up to #502 (already merged)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` after #502; touches only `sp-batch-report-view` (doc, tangled `.el`, tests). No conflict expected.\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-4a39fy`: the cloud proxy cannot rename a branch, so it needs the number prefix from Sia.\n\n## What changed\n\n- All tables of a report share their column widths, so columns line up across headings.\n- The Title column (`sp-batch-report-flexible-column`) takes what the others leave, so the columns fill the whole frame; it is narrowed first when the window is small.\n- BibTeX keys are cut after 45 characters (the lint limit) and the `BibTeX file` name is cut after it is listed (`sp-batch-report-truncated-columns`): cut with an ellipsis, not wrapped.\n- Other cells still wrap inside their column.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/sp-batch-report-view-test.el`: 20 tests, 19 pass, 1 skipped without Org. New: shared columns, Title widest and filling the row, keys and files cut not wrapped.\n- `sp-bibtex-zotero` tests pass; `sp-author-notes-bibtex` has the same 7 Org-path failures as before this change (Org does not load in the container).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex`: tables of different people have the same column widths\n- [ ] The table fills the frame; Title is the widest column\n- [ ] A BibTeX key over 45 characters ends in `…`; a long `.bib` name is cut, not wrapped\n- [ ] Resize the frame and `text-scale-adjust`: columns follow, keeping folds and drops\n- [ ] Zotero path report: its tables also line up with each other\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9bi8g2P4sdH8GttsS)_",
